# .agent/config.env -- repository facts for agent skills.
#
# Commit this file. It is parsed line-wise, never sourced: shell metacharacters
# are data, not code. Unknown keys are ignored with a warning; invalid values
# are dropped and the skill falls back to live discovery. A half-filled file is
# still useful, and a corrupt one cannot wedge a run.
#
# Generate it with:  .shared/scripts/bootstrap-repo.sh --dry-run
#
# NEVER put a token, password, proxy URL, hostname, or CA certificate path in
# this file. Those keys are refused outright. Machine-specific facts (CA bundle,
# cache roots, sandbox state) stay probed at runtime by agent-preflight.sh
# because they differ per developer, not per repository.

# owner/name of the GitHub repository.            shape: owner/name
AGENT_REPO_SLUG=example-org/example-repo

# Trunk branch that feature branches are cut from and merged into.
AGENT_BASE_BRANCH=main

# GitHub Projects (v2) board this repository's issues live on.
AGENT_PROJECT_OWNER=example-org
AGENT_PROJECT_NUMBER=7

# The board's single-select Status column, in board order.
AGENT_STATUS_VOCAB=Backlog,Ready,In progress,In review,Done

# Generator that last wrote the discovered onboarding facts; drift detection
# compares this stamp with the installed plugin.
AGENT_ONBOARDED_BY=agentkit/0.1.0

# Architecture decision records, relative to the repository root.
AGENT_ADR_DIR=docs/adr

# Allowed branch-name prefixes.                   shape: lowercase, comma list
AGENT_BRANCH_PREFIXES=feat,fix,refactor,docs,chore,test,perf,ci

# Where per-PR worktrees are created, relative to the repository root.
AGENT_WORKTREE_ROOT=.worktrees

# Optional. Comma-separated repository-relative path prefixes for generated
# artifacts. These are evidence categories for diff-facts.sh, not a size
# verdict; for example: generated/,openapi.json. The same list also tells
# gh-pr-state.sh which post-merge trunk-automation commits (a results-
# recording workflow, for example) must not stale a queued PR's base -- a
# base advance confined entirely to these prefixes reports stale=no, so
# merge-gate.sh does not block pr-to-green's merge gate on it.
# AGENT_GENERATED_PATHS=generated/,openapi.json

# Optional implementation-worker tier. These repository-wide defaults preserve
# the existing dispatch behavior; unsupported models still require explicit
# user authorization at the spawn gate. Values are parsed, never sourced.
# AGENT_WORKER_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# AGENT_WORKER_MODEL_FALLBACK=gpt-5.6-terra
# AGENT_WORKER_EFFORT=high

# Label taxonomy, so agents apply existing labels instead of inventing them.
AGENT_LABEL_TYPES=bug,feature,chore
AGENT_LABEL_AREAS=api,ui,infra
AGENT_LABEL_PRIORITIES=p0,p1,p2

# Automated review providers expected on pull requests. ADVISORY ONLY: the
# actual comment author still decides provider identity at review time, because
# this file cannot know a provider was disabled or renamed since it was written.
# One or more of: coderabbit, github-code-quality, none
AGENT_REVIEW_PROVIDERS=coderabbit

# Optional. Command wrapper agent-run.sh delegates to. Must live inside the
# repository and be executable. Equivalent to .agent/runner, which is also
# still honored.
# AGENT_REPO_RUNNER=tools/verify

# What this repository's verify commands actually are. Skills refer to them by
# NAME (`agent-run.sh --cmd test`), so no skill ever hardcodes an ecosystem.
#
# Values are argv: split on whitespace and exec'd directly. No shell is
# involved, so `;`, `|`, `&`, backticks, `$(...)`, and redirects are rejected
# rather than interpreted. For anything needing shell syntax, point
# AGENT_REPO_RUNNER at a script instead.
#
# The first word is the executable. A bare name is looked up on PATH; a name
# carrying a slash is a path, and like AGENT_REPO_RUNNER it must resolve inside
# this repository -- `..` and symlinks leading out are rejected.
#
# If a name is not declared here, agent-run.sh falls back to the declared
# runner invoked as `runner <name>`.
# AGENT_CMD_VERIFY=tools/verify
# AGENT_CMD_TEST=npm run test
# AGENT_CMD_LINT=npm run lint
# AGENT_CMD_TYPECHECK=npm run typecheck
# AGENT_CMD_BUILD=npm run build
